{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794819239,"nonce":"8lLDeu4ClVm+N/8Lwvh5x7QV1FI=","title":"Ordered images take node slots and follow the rows","message":"A batch's dynamic images with a paint order (images drawn through GpuPaintContext::emit_image, e.g. inside a cross-stream group) carry no node slot, so NodeRows::plan declines any batch with has_ordered_images. Give each the ordinal of the bound node it was painted under, a row when slots are given, and draw it through the rows (GPU: the table; CPU: the twin) with its clip split into the part that stays and the part that moves. Done when 'scroll grouped images, then stop' is in ON_ROWS on the table and the CPU rows.\n\nPart of d6c8230c7f2604cda9854e87e879842b181993174adc3e1f6f68e7910bb1e8e9.","files":null}]}